It was observed that the application restricts the modification of certain product parameters, including Product Code, Society Code, Customer Category, and Commercial Product, through the user interface after a product has been created. However, these restrictions are enforced only on the client side. By intercepting and modifying the HTTP request, a user can modify the values of these restricted parameters. The application accepts and processes the modified values without performing adequate server-side validation, allowing users to modify product parameters that are intended to be non-editable.

Validate submitted values against the application's business rules before updating the database.
